# PAM policy for remote login over RDP (sg-rdp-authd, ADR 0010).
#
# Deliberately the same stacks as a console login: a remote login must face the
# same password rules, lockout (pam_faillock, if configured) and account expiry
# as someone at the keyboard. Anything weaker here would make RDP the easy way
# in. The session stack is used when sg-rdp-authd starts the remote session
# (systemd-run PAMName=): logind registers it and the profile service runs.
@include common-auth
@include common-account
@include common-session
